<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is James Harden on $30.65m in 2026-27?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Harden is paid <strong>$30.65m</strong> because a former Most Valuable Player who still creates offense for a whole team is worth a large number, and 37 is old enough to bring it down.</p>
<ul>
<li>He has signed eight NBA contracts and three of them were worth more than <strong>$100m</strong>.</li>
<li><a href="/teams/houston-rockets/">Houston</a> extended him three times between 2012 and 2017, the last for <strong>$171.13m</strong>.</li>
<li>He was paid <strong>$39.45m</strong> last season, so this is a fifth less.</li>
<li>He led the league in scoring in three consecutive seasons and in assists twice.</li>
<li>The last year of this contract is a player option, so nothing past 2027-28 is settled.</li>
</ul>
<p>This is the lowest salary he has been paid since 2018-19.</p>

